## Minor findings (not fixed)

- `magic.rs` checks the demo address after the rate-limit hits, so a demo request takes a slightly different path than other addresses. The response body is the same, so this is low risk.
- `verify.rs` consumes a token before the demo check. A demo token cannot exist, because issuing one is refused, so this is only a theoretical concern.
- `find_or_create_user` and `create_account` treat any unique-violation as "account exists". A rare handle collision would show the same message. The handle is 12 random hex characters, so the chance is negligible.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=345

